# Feasibility assessment (idea-review-repo)

Verdict: feasible within budget. The study is tiny (150 samples, 4 features, 2 models). The risks are in the plumbing (Ibex vs local identity, 2-page limit, interval definition), not compute.

## Probed facts (2026-10-17, measured from the sandbox)
- OpenML id 61 is reachable from the sandbox (`https://www.openml.org/api/v1/json/data/61` -> 200) and from the Ibex login node (`https://www.openml.org/data/v1/download/61` -> 200). Compute-node network access was NOT tested.
- Ibex login `python3` (/home/$USER/miniforge3) has scikit-learn 1.5.0, numpy 2.1.2. The local sandbox venv has NO scikit-learn; an unpinned `pip install scikit-learn` gives 1.9.1. Different versions can change inner-CV/LogisticRegression numerics and break the "identical numbers" check.
- Ibex: SLURM, partition `batch` (CPU), account `pi-gaox`; /ibex/user/$USER/rw exists (contains other worlds' dirs: do not touch them). Jobs must be named with `$HT_RESOURCE_TAG` and registered with `ht-resource track ibex <jobid>`.
- NeurIPS 2026 template downloadable: https://media.neurips.cc/Conferences/NeurIPS2026/Formatting_Instructions_For_NeurIPS_2026.zip (neurips_2026.tex, neurips_2026.sty, checklist.tex). The .sty is not at the older media.neurips.cc/.../Styles/ URL (404).

## Risks and what to bound
1. Identical numbers across Ibex/local. Pin the same environment on both (create a venv/conda env locally with scikit-learn==1.5.0, numpy==2.1.2, scipy matching Ibex; record `pip freeze` and versions in both outputs). Single-threaded BLAS (OMP/OPENBLAS/MKL_NUM_THREADS=1), `random_state` fixed per repetition via an explicit seed list, deterministic solver. Define "identical" in advance: bit-exact per-fold accuracies and chosen k (compare with a hash/diff of the fold-level CSV), and report the max abs difference of the aggregate numbers if not. Different CPU microarchitectures can legitimately produce last-digit differences in lbfgs; if so report that honestly, don't tune to hide it.
2. Data provenance. Download dataset 61 from OpenML itself, once, on each side or ship one file with a recorded SHA-256; record version/hash of the downloaded data on both runs. Compute nodes may lack internet: fetch on the login node (or ship the file) and have the job read the local copy; the hash must match the local run's.
3. Statistics: 10x5 CV folds are not independent (overlapping training sets). A naive 95% t-interval over 50 folds is optimistically narrow. Pick one stated method (e.g. Nadeau-Bengio corrected resampled t-interval for the paired difference, or interval over the 10 per-repeat means) and state it in the table caption; do not present the naive interval as exact. Accuracy on 150 samples has granularity 1/30 per fold, so ties/zero difference in many folds are expected; note that the interval for the difference likely covers 0.
4. Inner CV for k: use a grid fixed in advance (e.g. odd k in 1..25 capped by inner training size ~96), inner stratified CV seeded deterministically, tie-break rule (smallest k) stated. Standardization, if used, must be inside the pipeline (no leakage). Logistic regression: multinomial, lbfgs, state C (default C=1 unless tuned in inner CV; tuning only one method would be an unfair comparison, so either fix C for LR or tune both).
5. Two-page limit in the NeurIPS template: with one figure and one table, text is tight. Does the limit include references / the NeurIPS checklist? The objective says "at most two pages"; safest is the whole PDF <= 2 pages, so drop the checklist and keep refs minimal (or put them within page 2). venue-repo/paper-repo must settle this; compile with TeX Live 2026 (pdflatex/latexmk), use the `final`/preprint option only if consistent with "submission template" (default anonymous submission mode is the safest reading).
6. Scheduling: Ibex queue is shared; batch partition currently busy (351/364 nodes allocated), so queueing may be minutes-hours. Submit the job early (the job itself should take well under a minute), then `ht-resource track`. Run the local job via `ht-resource run local-compute`; no network there, so data must be pre-fetched. Do not make the paper wait: request the Ibex run right after the code is fixed.
7. "Code that produced every number": the figure/table/report numbers must be generated from the fold-level result files by committed scripts; no hand-typed numbers in LaTeX (use generated .tex fragment or macros).

## Scope limits
Iris only, 2 models, accuracy only. No claim beyond this dataset; the paired difference on 150 samples is expected to be small relative to its interval. Out of scope: other metrics, hyperparameter studies, other datasets.
